  "reason": "The dominant finding is the large jump from singleprofile (best: 0.540, config_026) to multiprofile with avgpool (0.678, config_030), indicating that the profile/aggregation axis is the most impactful design dimension. The key uncertainty now is whether avgpool is sufficient or whether a transformer aggregation that models inter-profile interactions yields further gains. Config_020 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, weighted) is a clean single-variable comparison against config_030, changing only aggregation from avgpool to transformer while holding RNA encoder, image encoder, fusion, and profile setting constant. If transformer substantially outperforms avgpool, it signals that inter-profile modeling is a productive direction to exploit; if it is comparable or worse, it confirms that simple pooling captures most of the multiprofile benefit and we can redirect effort to other axes (e.g., image encoder or RNA encoder). Under a limited budget, isolating the aggregation mechanism in the already-promising multiprofile setting is the highest-information next step."
